def decorator(func):
    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
        username = kwargs.get("username")
        return func(username)
    return wrapper

@decorator
def hello(username):
    return f"Hello {escape(username)}!"

def escape(text):
    return text.replace("<", "&lt;").replace(">", "&gt;")
```
This code defines a decorator function `decorator` that takes a function as an argument and returns a new function with the same functionality, but with additional functionality to handle the mapping between URLs and functions. The `hello` function is defined inside the decorator and takes a single argument `username`. The `escape` function is also defined inside the decorator to convert special characters to HTML-safe sequences.

When the user navigates to the URL `/hello/username`, the `decorator` function is called with the URL as an argument, which in turn calls the `hello` function with the `username` value as an argument. The `hello` function returns a string with the text "Hello" followed by the value of the `username` variable, and then the `escape` function converts any special characters in the returned string to HTML-safe sequences.']

